<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
	<!--
	  Everything else in this app's Info.plist is generated from build
	  settings (GENERATE_INFOPLIST_FILE); this file exists only for the keys
	  that are dictionaries, which build settings cannot express.

	  NSAllowsLocalNetworking permits plain HTTP to localhost, .local names
	  and IP literals — nothing else. It is what lets a debug build talk to
	  `npm run dev` on a laptop. It is deliberately not
	  NSAllowsArbitraryLoads: that would turn off transport security for
	  novicetutor.com too, and App Review asks for a justification for it.
	-->
	<!--
	  Export compliance. The app uses only HTTPS and the standard encryption
	  iOS provides; it ships no cryptography of its own. Declaring it here
	  answers the question once instead of on every single upload.
	-->
	<!--
	  Audio only. Not `voip`: that mode exists so a PushKit push can wake a
	  terminated app straight into CallKit, and since iOS 13 a voip push that
	  is not reported to CallKit immediately kills the app. This app has
	  neither, so voip would be an unused declaration App Review asks about.
	  `audio` is what keeps the lesson audible when a student locks the phone
	  or checks a message. Video suspends on its own — iOS forbids background
	  capture, and the LiveKit SDK stops publishing the camera anyway.
	-->
	<!--
	  The launch screen, spelled out rather than generated. The generated one
	  is plain `systemBackground` — white on a light-mode phone — while the
	  first SwiftUI frame is near-black, so every cold launch flashed white
	  before the app appeared. `UIColorName` names a colour in the asset
	  catalog; the generation build setting silently ignored it.
	-->
	<key>UILaunchScreen</key>
	<dict>
		<key>UIColorName</key>
		<string>LaunchBackground</string>
	</dict>
	<key>UIBackgroundModes</key>
	<array>
		<string>audio</string>
	</array>
	<key>ITSAppUsesNonExemptEncryption</key>
	<false/>
	<key>NSAppTransportSecurity</key>
	<dict>
		<key>NSAllowsLocalNetworking</key>
		<true/>
	</dict>
</dict>
</plist>
